Fixed. The bug was in `skipValue()` in gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/JsonTreeReader.java:441-448 — after popping the skipped value, `stackSize` can reach 0 (e.g. skipping a top-level object), and the unconditional `pathNames[stackSize - 1]` / `pathIndices[stackSize - 1]++` indexed the arrays with -1, causing the `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`.

The fix guards the path bookkeeping so it only runs when the stack is non-empty:

```java
if (skippedName) {
  pathNames[stackSize - 2] = "null";
} else if (stackSize > 0) {
  pathNames[stackSize - 1] = "null";
  pathIndices[stackSize - 1]++;
}
```

Validation:
- `JsonTreeReaderTest` (both `testSkipValue_emptyJsonObject` and `testSkipValue_filledJsonObject`): 2/2 pass — skipping now leaves the reader at `END_DOCUMENT`.
- Full `gson` module suite: no regressions; the only failures are pre-existing date-locale/timezone tests (confirmed identical on the unmodified baseline via `git stash`).
